==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing F_PermissionMatrix removes all (Relationship × OperationKind) constraints from PermMatrix.allowed. Combined with F_OutcomeDeterminedByMatrix also cleared (or left consistent with injected violation), Alloy can freely assign any outcome to any access. The injection forces a compliance officer to have a Permitted GetRecord access, directly violating LeastPrivilege, FR_007 and FR_019.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_007_ComplianceContentBlindness, FR_019_ComplianceNoClinicContent, FR_018_AccessLogComplianceOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_007_ComplianceContentBlindness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_ComplianceNoClinicContent: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AccessLogComplianceOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamRelationshipCorrectness  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_CareTeamRelationshipCorrectness.als
    rationale: Clearing F_CareTeamRelationshipCorrectness severs the link between CareTeamClinician relationship and actual CareTeamMembership rows. The injection forces a clinician to be classified as CareTeamClinician (and therefore Permitted) on a record for which no membership exists, exactly the care-team gating bypass FR-004 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: FR_004_CareTeamGating, LeastPrivilege, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoteAuthorIsClinician  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_NoteAuthorIsClinician.als
    rationale: Clearing F_NoteAuthorIsClinician removes the structural constraint that only clinicians can author notes. The injection places a patient as a note author, which is exactly the write-privilege escalation FR-012 and data-model.md's author_role CHECK prevent.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnlyNotes, FR_012_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnlyNotes: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_NotesAppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditCompleteness removes the bijection between Access atoms and AuditEntry atoms. The injection forces an Access with no linked audit entry, which is the exact SC-001/SC-002 violation (a record access with no matching audit entry).
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompletenessCheck, FR_013_AuditCompletenessOneToOne, AppendOnlyAuditEntries
      - AuditCompletenessCheck: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_013_AuditCompletenessOneToOne: PASS (vacuous?)
      - AppendOnlyAuditEntries: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrectness  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AttributionCorrectness allows audit entries to record a different role or accessor than the actual caller. The injection forces an audit entry whose recorded accessor role differs from the user's actual role, violating FR-014's requirement that accessor_role be snapshotted accurately from the authenticated identity context.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectnessCheck, FR_015_AuditImmutableRetained, AppendOnlyAuditEntries
      - AttributionCorrectnessCheck: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditImmutableRetained: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnlyAuditEntries: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PatientOwnRecordCorrectness  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PatientOwnRecordCorrectness.als
    rationale: Clearing F_PatientOwnRecordCorrectness severs the link between PatientOwnRecord relationship and the patient's assigned_record_id. The injection forces a patient to receive Permitted access on a record that is not their assigned record, which is the cross-patient information disclosure FR-006 and SC-010 explicitly prohibit.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_006_PatientSelfAccessOnly
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_PatientSelfAccessOnly: FAIL (expected)

